{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 23, :comments ["<b>And they stoned him with a stone.</b> This teaches that if he died from one stone, they have fulfilled their obligation." "<b>And the children of Israel did.</b> From that day onward, this law regarding one who wounds his fellow. Another interpretation: <b>And the children of Israel did</b> — even for semikhah, even for postponement, even for hanging. <b>The order of the portion of Emor is complete.</b>"], :book :leviticus, :voice :chizkuni, :lang :en, :chapter 24, :notes {1 "Semikhah (leaning on an offering), postponement (of execution over a festival), and hanging (display of the executed) are referenced as other laws derived from Israel's acts of execution elsewhere in the Torah."}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T15:15:04.056334994Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}